The validation check for `upstreamPassing` currently only verifies that the number of granular fields in the upstream schema matches `DISPLAY_GATE_FIELDS.length`. To prevent silent mismatches if fields are renamed or replaced in the upstream schema, we should explicitly verify that the exact expected fields are present. Additionally, when validating the expected array field `granular_fields`, if the field is present but is not an array, we must record a validation failure (blocker) and process it as an empty array to prevent TypeErrors and ensure the system fails closed.

```javascript
  let upstreamFields = upstream.schema?.display_gate_contract?.granular_fields;
  if (upstreamFields !== undefined && !Array.isArray(upstreamFields)) {
    recordValidationFailure("granular_fields is not an array", { blocker: true });
    upstreamFields = [];
  } else {
    upstreamFields = upstreamFields || [];
  }
  const upstreamPassing =
    upstream.readModelValidator?.validator_status === "pass" &&
    upstream.readModelValidator?.issue === READ_MODEL_ISSUE &&
    upstreamFields.length === DISPLAY_GATE_FIELDS.length &&
    DISPLAY_GATE_FIELDS.every((field) => upstreamFields.includes(field));
```

